  "recipeDetail": "Comments from the Creator\nThis high-contrast, film-inspired recipe enhances the three-dimensional quality of a cat's eyes and fur. A subtle bluish-green cast in the shadows and highlights creates a slightly cool tone, while warm orange in the mid-tones softens the overall impression. Chroma is subdued to evoke the calm, nostalgic feel of vintage film photography. Especially, when the eyes catch the natural blue light of morning, their clarity deepens and the shadows and textures of the fur come to life. I recommend this recipe for close-up shots taken under soft window light, using morning backlighting to achieve a dramatic, expressive finish.\n",
